	<body bgcolor="#ffffff" text="#000000">
		<h1 class="largetext">Rodcetnife.org Forums</h1>
		<h2 class="normaltext">General Category => Blacklist => Topic started by: Nosterafu on February 25, 2004, 02:58:22 am</h2>

		<table width="90%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Nosterafu</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 02:58:22 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Heads up with this guy. Very dishonest person a guildie had purchased Breneaur from this mofo and leveled them from 62 to 65 epiced them and replaced the crap gear that they had with around 600k of gear to come on the othger day with the password changed and finding out that the original owner had went behind there back and changed the password through Sony&#039;s back door and asked to have them apped into apotheosis as Einalem&#039;s alt. Careful grouping with this A-hole because if he has ripped one person off you know its not beneath them to screw you.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 06:42:18 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Nost, you forgot to mention he did the Emp key for Ssra, as well as completed his spell book....<br /><br />If you sell your account, WALK AWAY... don&#039;t steal it back after someone else has put work into the character, that&#039;s just wrong.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rednight</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 09:04:08 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Yea thats pretty lame, I think you can change the account info rather then just the password to ensure that you keep the account.  Not completely positive on that tho.<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 09:08:05 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">If someone has the original CD keys, and original credit card information, they can take the account back at anytime.  It&#039;s just extremely dishonest to sell an account, then take it back after someone has already given you money, as well as invested their time and effort into developing the character further.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rednight</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 09:14:26 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Hopefully you can meet up with him at the next Fan fair and show him how you really feel ;D</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Nosterafu</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 11:52:21 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">your right Simplee I forgot about the emp key and Az buying HoV and all the spells this ass clown ignored to buy on his own.<br />Also real sweet work on his epic now hes epiced because he was to lazy to get off his ass and do it himself.(sounds like a good cleric to me)<br />That should be warning enough for anyone wanting to group with this clown that he probably sucks as a cleric if he doesnt care enough about him to epic him himself or make sure he is properly geared.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Bieroth</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 12:03:31 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">This Einalem/Breneaur guy is an ASS.  Bigtime ASS.  For anyone to lay claim on someone elses efforts is just down right lame.<br /><br />I know Az contacted the guild leader of Apotheosis to let his complaint towards Einalem/Breneaur be known....I&#039;m not sure what the GL had to offer for help towards this matter...but, if he doesn&#039;t act on it...I consider him in the shithead pile as well.<br /><br />Get a clue Einalem...your probably all of 13 yo, and don&#039;t have a clue in life...BUT, this is not how you treat a fellow gamer...especially someone like Azlani who puts others before himself consistantly.<br /><br />You know what happens when you screw with the a player like Azlani?  His army of friends he&#039;s been kind to in his path through Norrath will seek retribution....So hold onto that click stick you haven&#039;t earned....or you might find it lodged somewhere you won&#039;t find very comfortable....</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Rednight</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 12:09:07 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">/em grabs lawn chair <br />/em pulls up his cooler of beer<br /><br />Where is our evil villian Einalem/Breneaur?<br /><br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>simplee</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 12:51:29 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I spoke with Qadain briefly last night.  He was very approachable, and said he had been waiting for Einalem to log in so he could ask him about what was going on.  He said he would ask him to return the account to Azlani, but aside from that, and deguilding him, there wasn&#039;t much else he could do.<br /><br />I appreciate his approach.  As a guild leader, its his job to hear both sides of the story, and he&#039;s right, there isn&#039;t much beyond asking him to return it, and deguilding him that he can do.  I&#039;ve had good experiences with Apotheosis, how they handle this will speak volumes about their guild leadership.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Az</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 01:58:57 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">As an update to this unfortunate bit of drama...<br /><br />I logged on this afternoon to see Einalem online. I asked him if he had decided to return my account to me to which he responded that he had spoken to his friend (imaginary?) and talked him into giving me the account back. Supposedly his friend (cough) also admitted to selling this same account to another person for 60kpp and then stealing it back.<br /><br />Subsequently, he gave me the login info to the account (supposedly because he wanted to do the right thing - thanks to those who bombarded him with tells). I am now in the process of deleting the nodrop gear from the account and sacrificing the cleric. After all, due to the account having been so blatantly compromised for whatever reason and by whomever, it is now useless to me and the mode of operation switches more to loss management as opposed to asset preservation.<br /><br />All of my dealings with this piece of scum were via the telephone. If he has screwed anyone else contact me in game and I will hook ya up with his name and number. Contemplated posting it here but that is in bad taste and I am trying to handle this as maturely as I can given how angry I am.<br /><br />Incidentally, the guild leader of Apotheosis just sent me a tell in game and apparantly decided to remove Einalem from the guild over this issue (/cheer Qadain and apoth).<br /><br />End result... Einalem = scammer and a prick. Apotheosis = pretty cool based upon how they handled this.<br /><br />-Az<br /><br />Oh! Forgot to mention that he had removed the belt of thunderous auras from Breneaur prior to giving me the account back. Way to do the right thing lol.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Nosterafu</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 03:25:30 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">3 cheers for Apotheosis for doing the right thing very cool of you guys.<br />Sorry about all the crap Az but at least theres finality in this.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>EQSysquella</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 05:07:28 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">shady shady</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 05:27:24 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">That&#039;s the most you can expect out of a guild, so yeah, great way to handle it on Ap&#039;s part.  It&#039;s not like they can force the guy to give the account back.  All they can do is talk about it and guildremove him. <br /><br />I&#039;m surprised he gave it back.  He could have denied everything or just done the equivalent of &quot;neener neener! mine now!&quot;  Of course he might have had trouble getting into a high end guild on rodcet nife afterward.  Though that could still be a problem.  :)  <br /><br />I&#039;m sorry that happened to you, Az, and I can see why you&#039;re going to stop using the account even though you have it back now.  Who knows when this guy could just decide to steal back his account again, only this time jump servers or something?  Get what you can off of it and cancel the account.  :(</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Bieroth</b> on <b>February 25, 2004, 07:44:38 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">/applaud Qadain <br /><br />Thanks Apotheosis for doing what you can as a guild to do the &quot;right&quot; thing....<br /><br />Now wheres the damn belt!  That lil freak....</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Beltran</b> on <b>April 07, 2004, 06:27:44 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Einalem apped Tul-Acharn 4 days after all of these posts and has had spotty attendence in game.  I will be guild removing him now.  We do not tolerate such behavior in TA either.<br /><br />Thanks for the heads up. <br /><br />Beltran</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Callon</b> on <b>April 07, 2004, 06:31:15 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I posted in this thread then didn&#039;t notice that he applied to the guild I&#039;m in and after awhile got in.  I pay attention GOOD.   ;D<br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Medsolo</b> on <b>May 06, 2004, 02:57:20 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Howdy.  Just thought I would give everyone an update on this toon.  He has a low level toon named Wolfpets.  He was invited into the Fizzle Fiends and was a decent addition to the guild.  He told me his account had been hacked and his 65 FoT flagged cleric was deleted, so he was in the process of /petitioning to get him back.  Care to guess what the cleric&#039;s name was?<br /><br />Anyway, he got Breneaur back with no loss of level and with his epic back.  I had no idea about what was going on until Azlani sent me a tell.  Azlani was a member of the Fiends many moons ago and we have many mutual friends.  He gave me the lowdown and told me he didn&#039;t care what action I took, but that the Fiends should know who we had in the guild.<br /><br />I discussed it with the rest of the guild officers and we came to the unanimous decision that we didn&#039;t want someone with that kind of reputation in the guild.  He has been removed.  I enjoyed playing with him on the several occasions I grouped with him, and he seemed like a decent enough guy.  It is a shame.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>/-|verse Thule</b> on <b>May 07, 2004, 03:32:58 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">(http://people.cornell.edu/pages/tpm2/emeril_image.gif)<br /><br />Says,  <span style="font-size: 7;">BAM!</span></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re:Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Nosterafu</b> on <b>May 08, 2004, 02:53:09 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Damn wish Az still had the password for this doofus so we could sack him down to 46 again for EEs hehe</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Shredd</b> on <b>August 30, 2004, 04:14:03 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Hey all,<br />I&#039;m one of the many that got scammed from this person. I purchased not just the Breneaur account but the Einalem account as well. <br /><br />I just noticed on the EQ name change site that Einalem is now: Hazinson.<br /><br />Please beaware that these two accounts are tainted.<br /><br />regards,</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Hazinson</b> on <b>August 30, 2004, 11:34:18 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">    Actually I bought Einalem&#039;s first charactor , a wizard about a year ago. I played a wizard on Xegony in a big guild there. My wife talked me into selling him and the new owner moved him to legends. After about 3 months i couldnt take it any more and started searching for another wizard. I found Einalem for sale at ebay.  I did end up buying it but it was a shaky deal, I never received the disk&#039;s and key codes,  and everything seemd to be very scary. I thoght for sure i was gonna lose my money. In my opinion he wasnt very honest and I think he tryed to get  this account back also at one time. I also explained this to the officers of my guild when I joined becuase he was at one time a member there also.  I changed the name  to a similer name like my original cuz Einalem spelled backwards was his girlfriends name and he wanted to keep that name for a future rouge. Also when I took over account I wanted to change the name cuz his reputation wasnt good at all from what I was told.&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Hazinson Goldenheart</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Az</b> on <b>August 31, 2004, 12:03:38 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I can vouch for this. Hazinson is a wizard and the Einalem that I dealt with was a rogue.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Einalem /Breneaur</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Dravack</b> on <b>August 31, 2004, 04:25:13 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">I guess lesson learned here is to get one of those free accounts from Sony and do an account transfer on it immediantly.&nbsp; Little extra money, but much safer I suppose.</div>
					<br /><br />
